</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Performance with Varying Training Epochs</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report the performance of the proposed post-training method (ECGFounder-PT) and the baseline fine-tuning strategy (ECGFounder) across epochs on the PTB-XL all-71 task in Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.4 Performance with Varying Training Epochs ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bridging Performance Gaps for Foundation Models: A Post-Training Strategy for ECGFounder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Since the validation and testing sets show similar trends, we present the results from the testing set for clarity. This analysis underscores the robustness and generalization of ECGFounder-PT compared to ECGFounder.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#S4.F3.sf2" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.4 Performance with Varying Training Epochs ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bridging Performance Gaps for Foundation Models: A Post-Training Strategy for ECGFounder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a>, ECGFounder-PT consistently outperforms ECGFounder across both macro AUROC and macro AUPRC. The advantage is evident from the first epoch: ECGFounder-PT achieves a macro AUROC of 0.922 and a macro AUPRC of 0.384, compared to the baseline’s 0.762 and 0.118, respectively. This immediate superiority demonstrates the effectiveness of the post-training strategy in rapidly adapting the pre-trained model to downstream diagnostic tasks, leveraging prior knowledge more efficiently than the baseline.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The most notable difference lies in convergence dynamics and final performance. The baseline strategy exhibits a prolonged and unstable learning curve: its macro AUROC on the testing set rises gradually, peaking at 0.919 at epoch 16, but fails to stabilize, fluctuating between 0.901 and 0.919 from epochs 16 to 30. Similar oscillations are observed on the validation set, suggesting overfitting and limited generalization. In contrast, the proposed post-training strategy converges rapidly and smoothly to a higher, stable plateau. Macro AUROC surpasses 0.940 by epoch 8 and remains around 0.944 thereafter, with negligible variance. This stable convergence indicates that ECGFounder-PT effectively regularizes the optimization process, guiding the model toward a broad and generalizable optimum.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#S4.F3.sf4" title="In Figure 3 ‣ 4.4 Performance with Varying Training Epochs ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bridging Performance Gaps for Foundation Models: A Post-Training Strategy for ECGFounder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(d)</span></a>, a similar trend is observed for the more challenging macro AUPRC, which is more informative for assessing performance on imbalanced datasets. The baseline strategy exhibits slow and unsteady improvement, reaching a maximum test macro AUPRC of 0.368. In contrast, ECGFounder-PT achieves a rapid and substantial gain, stabilizing around 0.435. This 18.2% relative improvement is particularly clinically meaningful, reflecting a markedly enhanced ability to identify true positives in imbalanced datasets, a common scenario in real-world ECG diagnosis.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
